  "notes": "Bright, bouncy, hook-first commercial trap where the melody *is* the hook — so the melody register is the highest on this bench, `chordToneBias` is 0.75 and `loopVerbatim` is set, because an extremely memorable contour is one that repeats unchanged. Steel-pan/marimba timbre and Caribbean-leaning modal loops put `major` and `mixolydian` in the scale mix beside the minor, which is rare for a trap child. The bounce comes from `syncopation` 0.6 with `tresilloBias` 0.3 and a staccato 808 doing quick 16th repeats, and `snare.fullTimeVariantProb` 0.35 is the research's \"or 2&4 on the faster bounce cuts\" — the one parameter that lets this model leave half-time. Hand percussion is authored as congas, bongos and snaps on the offbeat. ⚠ The research gives two tempo poles (90–100 straight, 130–150 half-time); this model is the half-time one, because `session.halfTime` is a single flag and the faster pole is the same music counted twice.",
